227
00:15:00,180 --> 00:15:05,020
because if we're being honest, moral, good, Christian people,

228
00:15:05,020 --> 00:15:08,640
we're really good at making our sin not sound as bad as it actually is.

229
00:15:08,640 --> 00:15:11,380
Like we'd be like, yeah, I don't discriminate.

230
00:15:11,380 --> 00:15:13,080
Maybe I show favoritism.

231
00:15:13,080 --> 00:15:17,080
Maybe I value this group of people more than this group of people,

232
00:15:17,080 --> 00:15:19,320
but I don't discriminate against that group of people.

233
00:15:19,320 --> 00:15:26,140
But if we're being honest, we're actually true about what's happening in our hearts.

234
00:15:26,740 --> 00:15:33,080
I think more often than not, we might realize that sometimes we do discriminate

235
00:15:33,080 --> 00:15:38,040
against one group of people or another, one type of person or another.

236
00:15:38,040 --> 00:15:41,080
I like this definition for discrimination.

237
00:15:41,080 --> 00:15:47,620
Discrimination is when you look at a person's outside to determine their worth on the inside.

238
00:15:47,620 --> 00:15:54,900
Discrimination is when you look at a person's outside to determine their worth on the inside.

239
00:15:55,000 --> 00:15:59,560
And James gives us a real-world example that I think the church in Jerusalem was struggling with.

240
00:15:59,560 --> 00:16:01,020
It seems very specific.

241
00:16:01,020 --> 00:16:05,720
He says, when a rich person enters your congregation, when you can tell that they have money,

242
00:16:05,720 --> 00:16:07,200
when you can tell that they have value,

243
00:16:07,200 --> 00:16:12,760
when you can tell that they might add something to your life and your church,

244
00:16:12,760 --> 00:16:17,560
and you treat them differently than the type of person that walks in invisibly, outwardly,

245
00:16:17,560 --> 00:16:24,340
and it looks like they don't have much to offer, you're discriminating, you're showing favoritism.

246
00:16:24,340 --> 00:16:29,340
And let's just call it what it is.

247
00:16:29,340 --> 00:16:37,760
In America, discrimination is one of those sins that we've committed so blatantly by a majority of our nation for so long

248
00:16:37,760 --> 00:16:42,420
that I think in order to make ourselves feel better about the progress that we've made,

249
00:16:42,420 --> 00:16:45,140
we tend to not really look at that sin at all.

250
00:16:45,140 --> 00:16:47,820
We're like, well, discrimination is something we've struggled with in the past,

251
00:16:47,820 --> 00:16:51,900
but it doesn't really exist in our lives in the present.

252
00:16:52,320 --> 00:16:59,840
And it might not as blatantly look the same as it used to, but it still exists.

253
00:16:59,840 --> 00:17:04,920
I mean, think with me for just a second about your high school lunch table.

254
00:17:04,920 --> 00:17:12,920
I think the high school lunch table is a perfect illustration of how sinful hearts tend to gather together

255
00:17:12,920 --> 00:17:16,260
in tribes of people that make them feel safe and comfortable.

256
00:17:16,260 --> 00:17:22,180
We like to spend time with people that can bring something to the table for us.

257
00:17:22,240 --> 00:17:26,840
We like to spend time with people that can add value to our lives.

258
00:17:26,840 --> 00:17:32,180
And James is saying the kingdom of God is about showing value to everyone equally

259
00:17:32,180 --> 00:17:35,480
because Jesus has died for everyone equally.

260
00:17:35,480 --> 00:17:39,980
He's invited us all into this kingdom by his sacrificial love,

261
00:17:39,980 --> 00:17:43,260
and that love does not discriminate based on what's on the outside.

262
00:17:43,260 --> 00:17:47,120
That love does not discriminate based on what can be brought to the table.

263
00:17:49,240 --> 00:17:53,260
And so what ways might discrimination just show its face in our lives?

264
00:17:53,260 --> 00:17:59,960
Race is the example that comes to the forefront of our minds.

265
00:17:59,960 --> 00:18:07,280
And again, I think we tend to pretend like that doesn't exist anymore because we feel so much shame

266
00:18:07,280 --> 00:18:09,000
about how it existed in the past.

267
00:18:09,700 --> 00:18:13,000
But is that something that flips into your life?

268
00:18:13,000 --> 00:18:20,620
I think far more often we discriminate based on people that fit into our kind of cultural, socioeconomic status,

269
00:18:20,620 --> 00:18:22,360
what makes us feel comfortable.

270
00:18:22,360 --> 00:18:28,300
Or honestly, probably the worst one in the church today is our political preferences.

271
00:18:29,300 --> 00:18:37,560
I think we could flip James' example on its head where James says if you see someone coming in that has external wealth

272
00:18:37,560 --> 00:18:41,860
and somebody that doesn't and you treat them differently, there's discrimination.

273
00:18:41,860 --> 00:18:46,940
But I think we could even say for our church, if you see somebody that walks in with a T-shirt that says,

274
00:18:46,940 --> 00:18:47,920
don't tread on me,

275
00:18:47,920 --> 00:18:53,280
and then you see somebody that walks in with a T-shirt that has a rainbow flag on it,

276
00:18:53,280 --> 00:18:56,940
and you immediately make judgments about what that person is about

277
00:18:56,940 --> 00:19:00,420
and you discriminate against who you would rather spend time with,

278
00:19:00,420 --> 00:19:03,580
what you would rather invest in.

279
00:19:03,580 --> 00:19:10,540
Is it possible that discrimination is creeping into your heart?

280
00:19:10,540 --> 00:19:13,280
Is it possible that you're judging the external,

281
00:19:13,280 --> 00:19:16,200
you're judging what you can see,

282
00:19:16,200 --> 00:19:20,440
and you're choosing to add value to one more than the other?

283
00:19:21,960 --> 00:19:24,120
It happens so easily.

284
00:19:24,120 --> 00:19:25,260
I think about my own life.

285
00:19:25,260 --> 00:19:27,900
There's people that could ask for a meeting,

286
00:19:27,900 --> 00:19:30,500
and I would drop everything in my schedule tomorrow,

287
00:19:30,500 --> 00:19:31,560
and I would make time for that.

288
00:19:31,560 --> 00:19:34,240
And there's other people where I'm like,

289
00:19:34,240 --> 00:19:36,020
hmm, let me look at my schedule.

290
00:19:36,020 --> 00:19:36,700
I'll get back to you.

291
00:19:36,700 --> 00:19:40,700
Three weeks later, four weeks later, they reach out again.

292
00:19:40,700 --> 00:19:42,020
Hmm, you know, I've been really busy.

293
00:19:42,020 --> 00:19:42,780
Sorry about that.

294
00:19:42,780 --> 00:19:44,620
Let me check the schedule,

295
00:19:44,620 --> 00:19:46,160
and I'll get back to you.

296
00:19:46,160 --> 00:19:49,160
And far too often, if I'm really honest with myself,

297
00:19:49,600 --> 00:19:53,860
what is driving the motivation behind that decision

298
00:19:53,860 --> 00:19:55,900
is what I can get out of the relationship.

299
00:19:55,900 --> 00:20:02,460
And James is saying that doesn't demonstrate the values of the kingdom of God.

300
00:20:02,460 --> 00:20:04,420
What you can get out of a relationship,

301
00:20:04,420 --> 00:20:07,020
that is not following the example of Jesus.

302
00:20:07,020 --> 00:20:11,700
Jesus laid down his life for people that brought nothing to the table

303
00:20:11,700 --> 00:20:15,260
to demonstrate the love of the kingdom of God.

304
00:20:15,260 --> 00:20:21,300
Verse 4 summarizes this point so well.

305
00:20:21,300 --> 00:20:23,400
He says, when you do this, when you discriminate,

306
00:20:23,400 --> 00:20:25,580
when you show partiality,

307
00:20:25,580 --> 00:20:30,660
doesn't it reveal that you become a judge with evil thoughts?

308
00:20:30,660 --> 00:20:32,400
We're valuing the wrong thing.

309
00:20:32,400 --> 00:20:35,240
We're valuing what can be added to our lives,

310
00:20:35,240 --> 00:20:38,920
power, success, social approval, status, or acceptance.

311
00:20:39,700 --> 00:20:43,960
When we do this, we're trying to create for ourselves a sense of safety

312
00:20:43,960 --> 00:20:45,160
from our tribe.

313
00:20:45,160 --> 00:20:50,240
A sense of safety from the kingdom that we're actually living for.

314
00:20:52,160 --> 00:20:55,680
But oftentimes, that safety is built on discrimination.

315
00:20:55,680 --> 00:21:00,280
We build up our tribe by tearing down other tribes.

316
00:21:00,280 --> 00:21:04,700
And this type of safety is temporary and fleeting.

317
00:21:04,700 --> 00:21:08,660
If we treat people harshly to build up our own kingdom,

318
00:21:08,660 --> 00:21:10,340
you don't think there's another group of people

319
00:21:10,340 --> 00:21:12,160
that are stronger with more numbers

320
00:21:12,160 --> 00:21:15,300
that can tear down our tribe by building themselves up?

321
00:21:15,340 --> 00:21:19,220
You don't think that this isn't a rocks and stones type game we're playing?

322
00:21:19,220 --> 00:21:25,220
Discrimination might get you ahead with your tribe temporarily,

323
00:21:25,220 --> 00:21:29,860
but mercy will get you ahead with your king eternally.

324
00:21:29,860 --> 00:21:34,600
Discrimination, it might build you some status.

325
00:21:34,600 --> 00:21:38,080
It might get you some popularity in your group.

326
00:21:38,160 --> 00:21:40,980
It might make you feel secure for a while,

327
00:21:40,980 --> 00:21:43,740
but you are building up a kingdom that is temporary.

328
00:21:43,740 --> 00:21:48,220
You are building up a safety net that will go away.

329
00:21:48,220 --> 00:21:50,280
But the kingdom of God is eternal,

330
00:21:50,280 --> 00:21:52,300
and the kingdom of God is built on mercy.

331
00:21:52,300 --> 00:21:53,820
We're going to see later in this passage

332
00:21:53,820 --> 00:21:57,300
that James is going to put mercy in contrast with discrimination.

333
00:21:57,300 --> 00:22:03,120
And mercy is whenever we extend love and grace and compassion to people,

334
00:22:03,200 --> 00:22:04,880
whether or not they can earn it or not,

335
00:22:04,880 --> 00:22:07,340
whether or not they deserve it or not.

336
00:22:07,340 --> 00:22:13,040
Discriminating against people shows that we are valuing the wrong thing.

337
00:22:13,040 --> 00:22:17,840
Secondly, it shows that we're living for the wrong kingdom.

338
00:22:17,840 --> 00:22:19,620
James goes on in verse 5.

339
00:22:19,620 --> 00:22:21,540
He says,

340
00:22:21,540 --> 00:22:22,880
Listen, my beloved brothers,

341
00:22:22,880 --> 00:22:26,640
has God not chosen those who are poor in the world

342
00:22:26,640 --> 00:22:30,880
to be rich in faith and heirs of the kingdom

343
00:22:30,880 --> 00:22:33,780
which he has promised to those who love him.

344
00:22:33,780 --> 00:22:36,040
But you have dishonored the poor man.

345
00:22:36,040 --> 00:22:37,920
Are not the rich ones who oppress you

346
00:22:37,920 --> 00:22:39,720
and those who drag you into court?

347
00:22:39,720 --> 00:22:41,500
Are not they the ones who blaspheme

348
00:22:41,500 --> 00:22:44,200
the honorable name by which you are called?

349
00:22:44,200 --> 00:22:46,280
James says,

350
00:22:46,280 --> 00:22:47,080
Discrimination,

351
00:22:47,080 --> 00:22:50,140
treating people differently based on what they bring to the table,

352
00:22:50,140 --> 00:22:53,060
reveals that you are living for the wrong kingdom.

353
00:22:53,060 --> 00:22:55,600
He reminds them that the kingdom of God

354
00:22:55,600 --> 00:22:59,280
is built upon those who are poor in spirit,

355
00:22:59,280 --> 00:23:02,620
who are poor in this world but strong in faith.

356
00:23:02,620 --> 00:23:08,100
Think about the ways in which God has built his kingdom in the past.

357
00:23:08,100 --> 00:23:12,880
Abraham, the father of the nation of Israel,

358
00:23:12,880 --> 00:23:16,320
was a middle-aged guy living in his dad's basement.

359
00:23:16,320 --> 00:23:19,220
No real plan for his future.

360
00:23:19,220 --> 00:23:24,220
No children to give him any earthly value.

361
00:23:24,400 --> 00:23:26,980
He was just coasting through life.

362
00:23:26,980 --> 00:23:28,100
And God said,

363
00:23:28,100 --> 00:23:30,000
I see the faith in you.

364
00:23:30,000 --> 00:23:31,720
Not what you bring to the table.

365
00:23:31,720 --> 00:23:35,220
Not the family of origin that you come from.

366
00:23:35,220 --> 00:23:36,880
I see faith inside of you.

367
00:23:36,880 --> 00:23:40,120
I'm going to choose you to be the father of many nations.

368
00:23:40,120 --> 00:23:41,060
Think about Joseph.

369
00:23:41,060 --> 00:23:43,580
He was a know-it-all young kid

370
00:23:43,580 --> 00:23:45,380
that didn't fit in with the rest of his family.

371
00:23:45,380 --> 00:23:49,020
He just couldn't figure out the social dynamics.

372
00:23:49,760 --> 00:23:52,440
He just kept offending his brothers and his parents.

373
00:23:52,440 --> 00:23:55,200
And he kept pinning his dad against his brothers.

374
00:23:55,200 --> 00:23:57,180
And he was just this know-it-all kid.

375
00:23:57,180 --> 00:23:59,900
And God saw the faith in the life of Joseph

376
00:23:59,900 --> 00:24:03,540
and used Joseph to rescue the nation of Israel.

377
00:24:03,540 --> 00:24:06,180
Think about Moses.

378
00:24:06,180 --> 00:24:08,760
Moses was a convict on the run, hiding.

379
00:24:08,760 --> 00:24:11,720
God saw the faith in Moses.

380
00:24:11,720 --> 00:24:13,800
Moses said, I can't even talk in public.

381
00:24:13,960 --> 00:24:15,380
And God said, no, you're going to go.

382
00:24:15,380 --> 00:24:18,680
I'm going to use you despite of what you bring to the table.

383
00:24:18,680 --> 00:24:19,540
Think about David.

384
00:24:19,540 --> 00:24:21,400
David was a runt of the family.

385
00:24:21,400 --> 00:24:25,420
His own dad didn't even see any real potential in him.

386
00:24:25,420 --> 00:24:29,920
And God used him to establish the kingdom.

387
00:24:29,920 --> 00:24:31,420
Think about Jesus.

388
00:24:31,420 --> 00:24:36,860
A homeless man who wasn't anything special to look at.

389
00:24:36,860 --> 00:24:41,640
A man of sorrows acquainted with grief.

390
00:24:42,760 --> 00:24:46,640
This is the king of the kingdom that we live for.

391
00:24:46,640 --> 00:24:50,380
The kingdom of God is not about what you can bring to the table externally.

392
00:24:50,380 --> 00:24:54,240
The kingdom of God is about the faith that you have in your hearts.

393
00:24:54,240 --> 00:24:57,580
And when we choose to treat people based on what we can see externally,

394
00:24:57,580 --> 00:25:02,220
we're choosing to treat people based on not the values of the kingdom of God,

395
00:25:02,220 --> 00:25:04,940
but the values of this world.

396
00:25:06,860 --> 00:25:11,240
Oh, and contrary to belief, contrary to popular belief in American theology,

397
00:25:11,240 --> 00:25:14,580
none of those people I just discussed were white.

398
00:25:14,580 --> 00:25:19,300
And yet, you look at the paintings that we have of Jesus.

399
00:25:19,300 --> 00:25:21,860
Anyway, that's, I'm meddling there.

400
00:25:21,860 --> 00:25:22,620
I'm not going to do that.

401
00:25:22,620 --> 00:25:26,780
The kingdom of God is far more concerned with our faith,

402
00:25:26,780 --> 00:25:29,780
our internal faith than our external value.

403
00:25:29,780 --> 00:25:31,320
1 Corinthians chapter 1.

404
00:25:31,320 --> 00:25:32,520
Paul says,

405
00:25:32,520 --> 00:25:36,060
Brothers and sisters, consider your calling.

406
00:25:36,060 --> 00:25:38,980
Not many of you were wise from a human perspective.

407
00:25:38,980 --> 00:25:41,020
Not many of you were powerful.

408
00:25:41,020 --> 00:25:43,080
Not many of you were noble of birth.

409
00:25:43,080 --> 00:25:47,920
Instead, God has chosen what is foolish in the world to shame the wise.

410
00:25:47,920 --> 00:25:51,940
God has chosen what is weak in the world to shame the strong.

411
00:25:52,060 --> 00:25:55,500
God has chosen what is insignificant and despised in the world,

412
00:25:55,500 --> 00:25:57,860
what is viewed as nothing to bring to nothing,

413
00:25:57,860 --> 00:26:02,340
what is viewed as something so that no one may boast in his presence.

414
00:26:02,340 --> 00:26:04,620
This will preach itself.

415
00:26:04,620 --> 00:26:07,980
It is from him that you are in Christ Jesus,

416
00:26:07,980 --> 00:26:10,160
who became wise from God for us.

417
00:26:10,160 --> 00:26:13,200
He became our righteousness, our sanctification, and redemption

418
00:26:13,200 --> 00:26:15,240
in order that as it is written,

419
00:26:15,240 --> 00:26:19,940
let the one who boasts boast in the kingdom of God.

420
00:26:20,000 --> 00:26:23,120
The kingdom of God is an upside-down kingdom.

421
00:26:23,120 --> 00:26:29,200
The king of our kingdom doesn't discriminate based on what he can get out of you.

422
00:26:29,200 --> 00:26:33,100
Our king kneels down and washes the feet of tax collectors

423
00:26:33,100 --> 00:26:39,440
and goes to the cross for the very people that are choosing to kill him.

424
00:26:39,440 --> 00:26:43,980
This is the kingdom that we've been invited into.

425
00:26:43,980 --> 00:26:45,260
And so when we discriminate,

426
00:26:45,260 --> 00:26:49,520
when we choose to devalue people based on what they can bring to the table externally,

427
00:26:49,520 --> 00:26:52,340
based on the value that we can see from them externally,

428
00:26:52,340 --> 00:26:55,540
we are choosing to live for a different kingdom.

429
00:26:55,540 --> 00:27:00,340
We rank people and discriminate against them based on what they can do for us.

430
00:27:00,340 --> 00:27:06,360
James is saying that discrimination goes against everything that Jesus died to create.

431
00:27:06,360 --> 00:27:11,120
At best, when we show discrimination, we're a walking contradiction.

432
00:27:11,120 --> 00:27:16,520
And at worst, maybe we've been deceived into believing that we have a genuine relationship with God

433
00:27:16,520 --> 00:27:19,240
when we're just doing external moral behaviors.

434
00:27:19,240 --> 00:27:26,900
So maybe you're here and you've always felt other than.

435
00:27:26,900 --> 00:27:30,060
You never fit in socially.

436
00:27:30,060 --> 00:27:34,140
You never felt like you added much value to the table.

437
00:27:34,140 --> 00:27:36,140
You never measured up.

438
00:27:36,140 --> 00:27:37,380
You never fit the mold.

439
00:27:37,380 --> 00:27:38,200
You never...

440
00:27:38,200 --> 00:27:40,080
Think about the high school lunch table.

441
00:27:40,160 --> 00:27:41,340
You didn't even have a table.

442
00:27:41,340 --> 00:27:49,020
And Jesus is saying this kingdom is for you.

443
00:27:49,020 --> 00:27:55,780
Your value isn't based on external earthly situations.

444
00:27:55,780 --> 00:28:00,360
Your value isn't based on what people at your workplace say about you.

445
00:28:00,360 --> 00:28:05,200
Your value is based on your faith in the Lord Jesus Christ.

446
00:28:07,200 --> 00:28:19,180
I think far too often we preach a gospel in our churches that invite people to measure up, to live up to a certain standard that we've created.

447
00:28:19,180 --> 00:28:24,920
When the kingdom of God is about faith in Jesus, realizing that we bring nothing to the table.

448
00:28:24,920 --> 00:28:28,580
That Jesus brought everything to the table for us.

449
00:28:31,020 --> 00:28:43,280
Maybe you're here and you're realizing that deep down in the depths of your heart, far more often than you would like to admit, you prioritize building your earthly kingdom rather than your heavenly kingdom.

450
00:28:43,280 --> 00:28:50,000
Maybe you internally rank people based on what they look like, how much money they have, or what they can do for you socially.

451
00:28:51,040 --> 00:28:53,840
And let's let the Spirit of God this morning just convict us.

452
00:28:53,840 --> 00:28:55,960
Let's do what we talked about last week.

453
00:28:55,960 --> 00:28:58,320
Let's just let the Word of God tell us what is true.

454
00:28:58,320 --> 00:29:03,240
Not in guilt and shame, but in an invitation to something better.

455
00:29:03,240 --> 00:29:06,680
And let's take steps in the right direction.

456
00:29:06,680 --> 00:29:08,580
I love what Brian Loritz says.

457
00:29:08,580 --> 00:29:08,940
He says,

458
00:29:08,940 --> 00:29:15,440
Biblical love is inconveniencing yourself for the convenience of others.

459
00:29:16,440 --> 00:29:20,620
Biblical love is inconveniencing yourself for the convenience of others.

460
00:29:20,620 --> 00:29:24,920
And far too often, the way that we treat people is, what are they going to do for me?

461
00:29:24,920 --> 00:29:28,820
Not what can I do for them.

462
00:29:28,820 --> 00:29:32,460
Discrimination reveals that we're living for the wrong kingdom.

463
00:29:32,460 --> 00:29:36,780
And then finally, it reveals that we're prioritizing the wrong law.

464
00:29:36,780 --> 00:29:38,880
Verse 8, he says,

465
00:29:38,880 --> 00:29:45,040
If you really fulfill the royal law according to the Scripture, you shall love your neighbor as yourself.

466
00:29:45,040 --> 00:29:45,880
You are doing well.

467
00:29:45,960 --> 00:29:53,540
But if you show favoritism, if you discriminate, you are committing a sin, and you are convicted by the law of transgressors.

468
00:29:53,540 --> 00:30:00,280
Whoever keeps the whole law but fails in one point has become accountable for all of it.

469
00:30:00,280 --> 00:30:05,680
For he who said, do not commit adultery, also said, do not murder.

470
00:30:05,680 --> 00:30:12,320
If you do not commit adultery, but you murder, you have become a transgressor of the law.

471
00:30:13,840 --> 00:30:17,780
So James here, in this paragraph, is going to compare two different laws.

472
00:30:17,780 --> 00:30:22,420
He's going to compare the law of transgressors to the law of liberty.

473
00:30:23,420 --> 00:30:25,820
The law of liberty, we talked about it last week.

474
00:30:25,820 --> 00:30:28,420
The law of liberty is the gospel sets us free.

475
00:30:28,420 --> 00:30:32,660
The law of liberty says you cannot live up to the righteous standard of God.

476
00:30:32,660 --> 00:30:37,060
It says all have sinned and fall short and deserve the punishment of God.

477
00:30:37,060 --> 00:30:42,480
This is the law of liberty because Jesus died in our place for our sins.

478
00:30:42,740 --> 00:30:50,940
We have been set free from the requirements of the law, and we've been invited to live according to the royal law, which just says love God and love others.

479
00:30:50,940 --> 00:30:54,720
That's what we've been invited to because of what Jesus has done for us.

480
00:30:55,560 --> 00:31:05,680
But he says, so often, believers, what they want to do is they want to judge themselves by the law of liberty, and they want to judge other people by the law of transgressors.

481
00:31:06,740 --> 00:31:11,380
How hypocritical is it of us to say, we could never live up to this external standard.

482
00:31:11,380 --> 00:31:14,380
We've fallen short, but we've received the grace of God.

483
00:31:14,380 --> 00:31:19,280
But you come into this place, and you're not living up to the standards that I want you to live up to.

484
00:31:19,280 --> 00:31:27,900
How hypocritical is it for us to judge other people based on an external law when we've been judged by the grace and mercy of God?

485
00:31:29,040 --> 00:31:31,840
According to the law of transgressors, we are all guilty.

486
00:31:31,840 --> 00:31:36,480
We have all fallen short of God's standards, and the penalty for that sin is death.

487
00:31:36,480 --> 00:31:42,980
But the law of liberty says that Jesus lived a life that was perfect in light of the law of transgressors.

488
00:31:42,980 --> 00:31:48,860
He was righteous, and yet he paid our penalty by dying in our place for our sins.

489
00:31:48,860 --> 00:31:57,180
Christians, again, who discriminate, we want to be judged by the law of liberty while we judge others by the law of transgression.

490
00:31:58,240 --> 00:32:04,300
We want God to judge us with grace while we judge other people with the law.

491
00:32:04,300 --> 00:32:09,980
When we judge people based on the law of transgressors, the question that we ask is,

492
00:32:09,980 --> 00:32:14,600
how does this person measure up to a list of external rules that I get to control?

493
00:32:14,600 --> 00:32:18,180
And it leads us to selfish discrimination.

494
00:32:18,180 --> 00:32:25,580
How does this person measure up to what I think they should be, who I think they should, how I think they should live, what they contribute to me?

495
00:32:26,980 --> 00:32:32,760
And when we judge people based on the law of liberty, the only question that we have to ask is, are they my neighbor?

496
00:32:32,760 --> 00:32:42,900
That's the new way of living in light of the law of liberty is this royal law.

497
00:32:43,580 --> 00:32:56,540
Jesus fulfilled all of the laws perfectly so that we didn't have to get tripped up on how much we fail so that all we get to do now is learn to love God with all of our heart, soul, mind, and strength and learn to love our neighbor as ourself.

498
00:32:56,540 --> 00:32:59,080
I love how Vance Pittman puts it.

499
00:32:59,080 --> 00:32:59,400
He says,

500
00:32:59,460 --> 00:33:16,140
Far too often, we want to experience God's grace in our own life and then not distribute it to those around us,

501
00:33:16,140 --> 00:33:23,860
or at least only distribute it to the people that we want to, based on standards that we create on an economy that we live for.

502
00:33:23,860 --> 00:33:37,940
And it reveals to us that we're living for the wrong kingdom, that we're trying to build our kingdom on earth rather than building the kingdom of God on earth as it is in heaven.

503
00:33:39,540 --> 00:33:48,400
So I think James is saying here that discrimination reveals that we're valuing the wrong desires, that we're investing in the wrong things, that we're asking the wrong questions.

504
00:33:48,400 --> 00:33:57,500
It reveals that we're living for the wrong kingdom and that we're prioritizing the wrong law.

505
00:33:57,500 --> 00:34:10,900
It reveals, when we discriminate, when we treat people this way, it reveals that at best we're walking contradiction and at worst we've been deceived into believing that something's true of us that's not actually true of us.

506
00:34:10,900 --> 00:34:17,200
I was listening to another pastor preach the book of James earlier in the week and he said,

507
00:34:17,200 --> 00:34:28,780
The tension in preaching the book of James is that James is clearly trying to get moral religious people to realize that they don't actually have a relationship with God,

508
00:34:28,780 --> 00:34:33,400
that they're being deceived into believing that something's true of them that's not true of them.

509
00:34:35,000 --> 00:34:44,920
On the same note, when you do that, what often happens is genuine believers who are just struggling hear that with guilt and condemnation.

510
00:34:44,920 --> 00:34:49,860
And so there's this balance beam that I have to walk here when we talk about James,

511
00:34:49,860 --> 00:34:54,280
where like those of you that are genuine followers of Jesus being transformed by the inside out but are struggling,

512
00:34:54,280 --> 00:34:58,180
because we are all struggling, there's grace for you.

513
00:34:58,180 --> 00:34:59,800
There's forgiveness for you.

514
00:34:59,800 --> 00:35:04,460
This is James just helping you see how you're living in light of a different kingdom,

515
00:35:04,460 --> 00:35:09,140
that you've been invited into something so much better, and so just set that aside and move forward.

516
00:35:09,140 --> 00:35:16,200
But for those of us who have hardened hearts, who have never experienced the love and grace of God,

517
00:35:16,200 --> 00:35:22,780
he wants us to realize that, to stop living moral lives and to start receiving the grace of God,

518
00:35:22,780 --> 00:35:25,860
being transformed from the inside out, again, not in guilt and shame,

519
00:35:25,860 --> 00:35:28,320
but inviting us into something so much better.

520
00:35:29,800 --> 00:35:34,760
The famous C.S. Lewis quote, it's not in my notes, but it just covers it so well.

521
00:35:34,760 --> 00:35:36,000
We cover it all the time.

522
00:35:36,000 --> 00:35:38,020
Like, we've been invited into something better.

523
00:35:38,020 --> 00:35:45,220
The religion is like kids playing in the dirt when they've been invited to a vacation at the beach.

524
00:35:45,220 --> 00:35:54,160
Moral living is this thing that we say no to the beach because we like this sandbox that we get to play in,

525
00:35:54,160 --> 00:35:58,920
and we don't realize how much better the kingdom of God is than the kingdom of this earth.

526
00:35:59,800 --> 00:36:04,420
He goes on in verse 12 and 13 to wrap it all up.

527
00:36:05,820 --> 00:36:06,440
He says,

528
00:36:06,440 --> 00:36:15,260
So speak and so act as those who are to be judged under the law of liberty.

529
00:36:15,260 --> 00:36:15,540
He's saying,

530
00:36:15,540 --> 00:36:20,200
If you perceive the grace of God, the forgiveness of God, extend that grace and forgiveness to others,

531
00:36:20,200 --> 00:36:23,620
not based on what they bring to the table, but equally to all people.

532
00:36:25,600 --> 00:36:31,000
For judgment is without mercy to the one who has shown no mercy.

533
00:36:31,000 --> 00:36:34,780
And mercy triumphs over judgment.

534
00:36:34,780 --> 00:36:35,140
He says,

535
00:36:35,140 --> 00:36:36,780
Don't live a contradictory life.

536
00:36:36,780 --> 00:36:40,620
Don't judge people based on the law of external,

537
00:36:40,620 --> 00:36:43,000
when you've received forgiveness for your sins,

538
00:36:43,000 --> 00:36:45,920
when you've been extended to grace through the law of liberty.

539
00:36:48,120 --> 00:36:53,620
Christ demonstrated his love for you in that while you were in rebellion to him and had nothing to offer,

540
00:36:53,620 --> 00:36:55,080
had nothing to bring to the table.

541
00:36:55,080 --> 00:36:57,700
He laid down his life for you.

542
00:36:57,700 --> 00:37:02,880
And you've been invited to extend that same grace and love to other people when they don't deserve it,

543
00:37:02,880 --> 00:37:04,440
when they're not bringing something to the table.

544
00:37:04,440 --> 00:37:07,020
Not only this, like this is the upside down kingdom.

545
00:37:07,020 --> 00:37:09,620
Sometimes not only are they not bringing something to the table,

546
00:37:09,620 --> 00:37:12,060
but they're bringing something negative to the table.

547
00:37:12,060 --> 00:37:17,180
This is where Jesus tells us to love our enemies and to pray for those who persecute you.

548
00:37:17,180 --> 00:37:23,740
Not only are we supposed to extend grace equally to everyone until they wrong us,

549
00:37:23,740 --> 00:37:30,040
but even after they wrong us, we continue to extend grace and mercy and love

550
00:37:30,040 --> 00:37:35,080
because that is the value of the king who came to show grace and mercy and love to us

551
00:37:35,080 --> 00:37:37,660
when we were his enemies, when we were far from him,

552
00:37:37,660 --> 00:37:40,360
when we were in rebellion to him.

553
00:37:40,360 --> 00:37:42,220
Jesus hung on the cross.

554
00:37:43,820 --> 00:37:49,580
Roman soldiers were laughing at the bottom of it, gambling over his clothes.

555
00:37:49,580 --> 00:37:50,020
And he says,

556
00:37:50,020 --> 00:37:53,320
Forgive them, Father, for they know not what they do.

557
00:37:53,320 --> 00:37:56,940
This is the example of our king.

558
00:37:56,940 --> 00:38:01,900
This is the value of the kingdom that we've been invited to live into.

559
00:38:03,660 --> 00:38:09,280
And so when we discriminate against others based on what we think they bring to the table,

560
00:38:09,280 --> 00:38:10,960
what we think they offer,

561
00:38:10,960 --> 00:38:14,580
we're showing that we value,

562
00:38:14,580 --> 00:38:17,920
we're living for a value system of a totally different kingdom.

563
00:38:17,920 --> 00:38:22,500
Finally, I love the summary statement at the end, verse 13.

564
00:38:23,380 --> 00:38:28,560
Here's the deal.

565
00:38:28,560 --> 00:38:34,400
We might get ahead temporarily using judgment as our main source of, as our main economy.

566
00:38:34,400 --> 00:38:41,060
We might be able to use judgment to get ahead, to build our little kingdom for a while.

567
00:38:41,060 --> 00:38:46,260
But eventually, that's going to bite us because when we judge others,

568
00:38:46,260 --> 00:38:48,800
they're going to judge us by the same standards that we judge them.

569
00:38:51,340 --> 00:38:56,080
James is saying, ultimately, mercy is going to triumph over judgment.

570
00:38:56,080 --> 00:39:00,920
Let's be a people who live in light of the kingdom now

571
00:39:00,920 --> 00:39:04,720
as we wait for Jesus to bring it to earth once and for all.

572
00:39:04,720 --> 00:39:10,200
So again, if you're here and you've always judged yourself harshly,

573
00:39:10,200 --> 00:39:14,700
you've always felt like you didn't have anything to offer anybody,

574
00:39:14,700 --> 00:39:16,760
always felt less than,

575
00:39:16,760 --> 00:39:21,120
man, the kingdom of God is for you.

576
00:39:21,960 --> 00:39:25,520
You've been invited to sit at the table of King Jesus.

577
00:39:25,520 --> 00:39:30,380
He laid down his life to demonstrate that you are worthy of his affection,

578
00:39:30,380 --> 00:39:32,520
that you are worthy of his sacrifice.

579
00:39:32,520 --> 00:39:35,060
And it doesn't matter what anybody else has to say about you.

580
00:39:35,060 --> 00:39:40,320
The King of the universe laid down his life to demonstrate your value.

581
00:39:40,320 --> 00:39:43,000
You've been invited to sit at the table.

582
00:39:44,920 --> 00:39:52,560
If you're here and you've received that grace and that mercy and you're realizing that you don't always extend it to others,

583
00:39:52,560 --> 00:39:55,540
and just receive that conviction,

584
00:39:55,540 --> 00:40:02,080
choose to believe that what God says is better and take steps of obedience in the right direction,

585
00:40:02,080 --> 00:40:05,700
not out of shame and guilt, but out of an invitation to something better.

586
00:40:07,300 --> 00:40:08,840
And for all of us,

587
00:40:08,840 --> 00:40:13,980
let this be a reminder that God's kingdom is an upside-down kingdom.

588
00:40:13,980 --> 00:40:22,180
It does not discriminate by power, skill, social status, race, political party, or any other external reality.

589
00:40:24,820 --> 00:40:30,840
It's what Revelation says about the kingdom of God in Revelation chapter 7, verse 9 and 10.

590
00:40:30,840 --> 00:40:31,740
John says,

591
00:40:32,440 --> 00:40:38,960
And for this I looked and behold a great multitude that no one could number from every nation,

592
00:40:38,960 --> 00:40:42,620
from all tribes and peoples and languages,

593
00:40:42,620 --> 00:40:46,860
from every political party and socioeconomic status,

594
00:40:46,860 --> 00:40:49,160
from every area of life,

595
00:40:49,160 --> 00:40:54,920
standing before the throne and before the lamb clothed in white robes with palm branches in their hands,

596
00:40:54,920 --> 00:40:56,360
crying out with a loud voice,

597
00:40:56,620 --> 00:41:03,640
salvation belongs to our God who sits on the throne and to the lamb.

598
00:41:03,640 --> 00:41:07,420
This is the kingdom of God.

599
00:41:07,420 --> 00:41:11,900
There's a table for everyone who would receive it.

600
00:41:11,900 --> 00:41:15,400
You've been invited to the table of God through the sacrifice of Jesus.

601
00:41:15,400 --> 00:41:17,900
All you have to do is receive it.

602
00:41:17,900 --> 00:41:25,060
So I can't think of a better way for us to end our time this morning than to take communion together.

603
00:41:25,440 --> 00:41:31,120
This communion is a reminder that we've been invited to the table

604
00:41:31,120 --> 00:41:38,440
and that all we have to do is take the cup to eat the bread, to drink the wine

605
00:41:38,440 --> 00:41:43,380
that represents Christ's body broken for us, his blood shed for us.

606
00:41:43,380 --> 00:41:46,360
What better reminder that we've all been invited.

607
00:41:46,360 --> 00:41:49,580
But there's a seat for anyone who would sit down.

608
00:41:49,580 --> 00:41:52,120
There's a passage in Revelation that says,

609
00:41:52,120 --> 00:41:55,840
After God brings his kingdom down to earth, the gate is always open.

610
00:41:55,840 --> 00:42:02,700
Like it's a reminder that the table has been prepared by the sacrifice of Jesus

611
00:42:02,700 --> 00:42:05,440
and it's for everyone who would receive it.

612
00:42:05,440 --> 00:42:09,540
So if you're here and you've received that,

613
00:42:09,540 --> 00:42:13,760
you believe that you've fallen short of God's standard

614
00:42:13,760 --> 00:42:20,440
and that the only way that you deserve a seat at the table is through the sacrifice of Christ.

615
00:42:20,440 --> 00:42:24,380
And here in a minute we're going to take communion together.

616
00:42:24,380 --> 00:42:28,500
But maybe you're here and deep down in your heart

617
00:42:28,500 --> 00:42:31,540
you think you deserve a seat at the table because of your pedigree.

618
00:42:31,540 --> 00:42:36,740
Because of who you are and how much better you are than other people.

619
00:42:36,880 --> 00:42:39,020
You play this moral-religious comparison game.

620
00:42:39,020 --> 00:42:41,500
These are the type of people that James is saying,

621
00:42:41,500 --> 00:42:42,760
Don't be deceived.

622
00:42:42,760 --> 00:42:44,380
That's not the kingdom.

623
00:42:44,380 --> 00:42:48,840
That's moral religion that won't get you anywhere in the end.

624
00:42:48,840 --> 00:42:52,240
Don't waste your time checking boxes

625
00:42:52,240 --> 00:42:56,160
when you've been invited to feast at the table of the Lord.

626
00:42:56,160 --> 00:42:58,400
So maybe that's you.

627
00:42:58,400 --> 00:43:02,960
Again, God's inviting you to the table.

628
00:43:02,960 --> 00:43:05,640
He's extended grace that you don't deserve.

629
00:43:06,880 --> 00:43:08,920
And this is what we've been invited to.

630
00:43:08,920 --> 00:43:10,520
So if you're not a follower of Jesus

631
00:43:10,520 --> 00:43:12,620
and you hear that invitation today

632
00:43:12,620 --> 00:43:14,320
and you want to receive that invitation,

633
00:43:14,320 --> 00:43:16,840
that invitation is received by faith.

634
00:43:16,840 --> 00:43:19,160
There's nothing special that you have to do.

635
00:43:19,160 --> 00:43:19,880
And I would say,

636
00:43:19,880 --> 00:43:20,940
I would say,

637
00:43:20,940 --> 00:43:22,160
in my opinion,

638
00:43:22,160 --> 00:43:23,920
there's no better way for you to receive that

639
00:43:23,920 --> 00:43:25,840
than to take communion for the first time

640
00:43:25,840 --> 00:43:30,480
as a public expression of the faith

641
00:43:30,480 --> 00:43:32,280
that you're committing to Jesus today.

642
00:43:32,280 --> 00:43:35,160
So this is for those of us

643
00:43:35,160 --> 00:43:36,940
that we consider ourselves followers of Jesus

644
00:43:36,940 --> 00:43:40,100
as a reminder that we've been invited to the table

645
00:43:40,100 --> 00:43:41,520
through the sacrifice of Jesus.

646
00:43:41,520 --> 00:43:43,240
For those of you that would consider that true

647
00:43:43,240 --> 00:43:44,780
about yourselves this morning,

648
00:43:44,780 --> 00:43:45,800
let's take the wafer

649
00:43:45,800 --> 00:43:48,140
that represents Christ's body broken for us.

650
00:43:57,620 --> 00:43:58,820
Let's drink the juice

651
00:43:58,820 --> 00:44:01,780
that represents Christ's blood said for us.

652
00:44:01,780 --> 00:44:11,680
Let's pray with me.

653
00:44:11,680 --> 00:44:17,140
Father, we thank you so much

654
00:44:17,140 --> 00:44:19,940
for the invitation to sit at your table

655
00:44:19,940 --> 00:44:24,280
to eat your body and drink your blood.

656
00:44:24,280 --> 00:44:26,300
It sounds really weird.

657
00:44:26,300 --> 00:44:31,400
But it's a reminder of what it costs,

658
00:44:31,400 --> 00:44:32,860
the price that you paid

659
00:44:32,860 --> 00:44:36,080
in order to buy for us a seat at the table.

660
00:44:36,080 --> 00:44:39,340
God, may we not waste the grace and mercy

661
00:44:39,340 --> 00:44:40,560
that you've extended to us

662
00:44:40,560 --> 00:44:42,280
by not extending it to other people.

663
00:44:43,880 --> 00:44:45,000
And may we not be a people

664
00:44:45,000 --> 00:44:47,120
that live in contradiction.

665
00:44:47,120 --> 00:44:49,300
May we be a people

666
00:44:49,300 --> 00:44:50,240
where our lives

667
00:44:50,240 --> 00:44:51,900
are slowly but surely

668
00:44:51,900 --> 00:44:53,500
lining up with the values

669
00:44:53,500 --> 00:44:54,580
of the kingdom of God.

670
00:44:54,580 --> 00:44:57,100
That we are slowly but surely

671
00:44:57,100 --> 00:44:58,580
being conformed to the image

672
00:44:58,580 --> 00:44:59,500
of Jesus

673
00:44:59,500 --> 00:45:00,960
falling in line

674
00:45:00,960 --> 00:45:02,500
with the way that you designed

675
00:45:02,500 --> 00:45:03,200
for us

676
00:45:03,200 --> 00:45:04,580
to live.

677
00:45:04,580 --> 00:45:06,060
And God,

678
00:45:06,060 --> 00:45:06,700
through that,

679
00:45:06,700 --> 00:45:07,380
may the kingdom

680
00:45:07,380 --> 00:45:09,040
of God be visible

681
00:45:09,040 --> 00:45:10,180
in the city of Winchester

682
00:45:10,180 --> 00:45:10,940
as it is

683
00:45:10,940 --> 00:45:12,940
in heaven. In Jesus' name

684
00:45:12,940 --> 00:45:14,560
I pray. Amen.
